Notebook[{
Cell["sl2cfoam++ in Mathematica", "Title"],

Cell["A complete, self-contained example. Build the Mathematica API using docs/mathematica.md, then evaluate the input cells in order with Shift+Enter. All spins and intertwiners are doubled integers. The default calculation uses physical spin j = 1/2 and cutoff 2.", "Text"],

Cell["Load the package", "Section"],

Cell["This cell looks for build-mathematica beside the repository examples directory. For another build or an installed package, set SL2CFOAMXX_MATHEMATICA_PACKAGE_DIR to the full SL2CfoamXX package directory before starting the kernel, or put its parent on $Path. Restart the kernel after rebuilding the native library.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["Module[{package = Environment[\"SL2CFOAMXX_MATHEMATICA_PACKAGE_DIR\"], local},\n    If[StringQ[package] && package =!= \"\",\n        Get[FileNameJoin[{package, \"Kernel\", \"init.m\"}]],\n        local = FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"build-mathematica\",\n            \"mathematica\", \"SL2CfoamXX\"}];\n        If[DirectoryQ[local],\n            Get[FileNameJoin[{local, \"Kernel\", \"init.m\"}]],\n            Needs[\"SL2CfoamXX`\"]\n        ]\n    ]\n];"], "Input", InitializationCell -> True],

Cell[BoxData["BuildInfo[]"], "Input"],

Cell["Boundary geometry", "Section"],

Cell["The built-in Euclidean preset supplies twenty {theta, phi} pairs in radians and closes for equal boundary spins. The Lorentzian preset is $LorentzianBoundaryAngles; it closes for doubled spins {10,10,10,10,4,4,4,4,4,4} and common positive scalings. Both follow canonical oriented-normal order, with a separate local frame at each node. Assign a preset to your own variable before editing.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["(* The library preset contains twenty {theta,phi} pairs in radians,\n   in canonical oriented-normal order. This copy can be edited locally. *)\n$SL2CfoamXXExampleAngles = $EuclideanBoundaryAngles;"], "Input", InitializationCell -> True],

Cell["Complete calculation", "Section"],

Cell["RunSL2CfoamXXExample[backend, twoJ, cutoff] computes fixed, coherent and full-tensor amplitudes. It checks closure, an independent small-spin reference, agreement between a fixed amplitude and a tensor entry, a save/load/map round trip, and both the direct coefficient overload and the Mathematica contraction with five coefficient vectors. The node permutations are required by the tensor recoupling bases.", "Text"],

Cell["The function also collects progress events, creates an independent dense tensor copy, and contracts two rank-five tensors over four axes. It uses a fresh temporary cache directory and removes it on completion or failure; returned tensors and arrays are held in memory. Its configuration explicitly selects gamma_j_p1 and disables coherent pruning for the reference comparison.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["RunSL2CfoamXXExample[backend_:\"CPU\", twoJ_:1, cutoff_:2] := Module[\n    {directory, config, spins, intertwiners, tensor, array, indices, fixed,\n     coherent, coefficientAmplitude, closure, coefficients, nodeSpins, nodeRows, events = {},\n     path, loaded, mapped, copy, rows, contracted, matrix, check, available},\n    check[value_] := If[FailureQ[value], Throw[value, \"ExampleFailure\"], value];\n    available = BackendAvailableQ[backend];\n    If[FailureQ[available], Return[available]];\n    If[!TrueQ[available],\n        Return[Failure[\"BackendUnavailable\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n            \"The requested backend is unavailable; GPU needs a CUDA build and compatible device.\"|>]]];\n    directory = CreateDirectory[];\n    WithCleanup[Null,\n        Catch[\n            config = check[DefaultConfig[]];\n            config[\"Backend\"] = backend;\n            config[\"CPUThreads\"] = 2;\n            config[\"ProgressBar\"] = True;\n            config[\"Verbosity\"] = \"summary\";\n            (* Explicit convention for the reference; the default is gamma_j. *)\n            config[\"SimplicityConstraint\"] = \"gamma_j_p1\";\n            config[\"Tensors\"] = Join[config[\"Tensors\"], <|\n                \"Directory\" -> directory, \"Storage\" -> \"in_memory_sym\",\n                \"ReuseExisting\" -> False|>];\n            config[\"CoherentAmplitude\"] = Join[config[\"CoherentAmplitude\"],\n                <|\"PruningRatio\" -> 0.|>];\n            check[Configure[config]];\n\n            (* All labels are doubled integers: 1 means physical j=1/2. *)\n            spins = ConstantArray[twoJ, 10];\n            intertwiners = ConstantArray[0, 5];\n            tensor = check[ComputeFullTensor[spins, cutoff, 1.2,\n                \"Backend\" -> backend, \"ProgressFunction\" -> (AppendTo[events, #] &)]];\n            indices = check[IndicesFromIntertwiners[spins, intertwiners]];\n            fixed = check[ComputeAmplitude[spins, intertwiners, cutoff, 1.2]];\n            If[Abs[check[TensorValue[tensor, indices]] - fixed] > 5.*^-10 Abs[fixed],\n                Throw[Failure[\"NumericalMismatch\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n                    \"Fixed amplitude and tensor entry disagree.\"|>], \"ExampleFailure\"]];\n            closure = check[CheckClosure[spins, $SL2CfoamXXExampleAngles]];\n            If[!TrueQ[closure[\"AllClosed\"]],\n                Throw[Failure[\"ClosureFailure\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n                    \"The example boundary does not close.\"|>], \"ExampleFailure\"]];\n            coherent = check[ComputeCoherentAmplitude[spins, cutoff, 1.2,\n                $SL2CfoamXXExampleAngles, \"Backend\" -> backend,\n                \"ProgressFunction\" -> (AppendTo[events, #] &)]];\n            If[twoJ == 1 && cutoff == 2 &&\n                Abs[coherent - (-1.6748256353857123*^-10 + 1.2973143587300214*^-10 I)] > 5.*^-19,\n                Throw[Failure[\"NumericalMismatch\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n                    \"Coherent amplitude differs from the independent reference.\"|>], \"ExampleFailure\"]];\n\n            (* Normal gives an independent, ordinary packed Mathematica array.\n               Mathematica positions start at 1, as do the returned indices. *)\n            array = check[Normal[tensor]];\n            Print[\"Shape: \", Dimensions[tensor], \"; first slice shape: \", Dimensions[array[[1]]]];\n            copy = check[DenseCopyTensor[tensor]];\n            check[SetTensorValue[copy, indices, 0.]];\n            Print[\"Copy changed independently: \", TensorValue[copy, indices] == 0.];\n\n            path = FileNameJoin[{directory, \"vertex.sl2cxx\"}];\n            check[SaveTensor[tensor, path]];\n            loaded = check[LoadTensor[path]];\n            mapped = check[MapTensor[path]]; (* read-only by default *)\n            If[check[Normal[loaded]] =!= array || check[Normal[mapped]] =!= array,\n                Throw[Failure[\"PersistenceMismatch\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n                    \"Saved tensor values changed.\"|>], \"ExampleFailure\"]];\n\n            (* Each coefficient vector follows its tensor recoupling basis.\n               The permutations below are essential, including at nodes 2/5. *)\n            nodeSpins = {{1,2,3,4},{5,6,7,1},{8,9,2,5},{10,3,6,8},{4,7,9,10}};\n            nodeRows = {{1,2,3,4},{6,7,8,5},{11,12,9,10},{16,13,14,15},{17,18,19,20}};\n            coefficients = Table[check[ComputeCoherentCoefficients[\n                spins[[nodeSpins[[n]]]], $SL2CfoamXXExampleAngles[[nodeRows[[n]]]]]], {n,5}];\n            (* Supply the five vectors directly; entries are neither conjugated\n               nor normalized, and no closure check uses this form. *)\n            coefficientAmplitude = check[ComputeCoherentAmplitude[spins, cutoff, 1.2,\n                Sequence @@ coefficients, \"Backend\" -> backend,\n                \"ProgressFunction\" -> (AppendTo[events, #] &)]];\n            If[Abs[coefficientAmplitude - coherent] > 5.*^-9 Max[Abs[coherent],10.^-300],\n                Throw[Failure[\"ContractionMismatch\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n                    \"Angle and coefficient overloads disagree.\"|>], \"ExampleFailure\"]];\n            (* Dot contracts the last tensor axis with each vector in turn. *)\n            contracted = Fold[Dot, array, Reverse[coefficients]];\n            If[Abs[contracted - coherent] > 5.*^-9 Max[Abs[coherent],10.^-300],\n                Throw[Failure[\"ContractionMismatch\", <|\"MessageTemplate\" ->\n                    \"Mathematica and native coherent contractions disagree.\"|>], \"ExampleFailure\"]];\n            (* T[a,b,c,d,e] U[f,b,c,d,e] -> M[a,f], using packed BLAS arrays.\n               A second computed tensor could replace the second rows here. *)\n            rows = ArrayReshape[array, {First[Dimensions[array]], Times @@ Rest[Dimensions[array]]}];\n            matrix = rows . Transpose[rows];\n            Print[\"sl2cfoam++ \", LibraryVersion[], \"; backend: \", backend];\n            Print[\"Fixed: \", ToString[fixed, InputForm], \"; coherent: \", ToString[coherent, InputForm]];\n            Print[\"Mathematica contraction: \", ToString[contracted, InputForm]];\n            Print[\"Tensor/tensor contraction shape: \", Dimensions[matrix]];\n            Print[\"Stored values: \", TensorMetadata[tensor][\"StoredValues\"],\n                \"; progress events: \", Length[events]];\n            <|\"Tensor\" -> tensor, \"Array\" -> array, \"FixedAmplitude\" -> fixed,\n              \"CoherentAmplitude\" -> coherent, \"CoefficientAmplitude\" -> coefficientAmplitude,\n              \"Closure\" -> closure,\n              \"Coefficients\" -> coefficients, \"Contraction\" -> matrix,\n              \"ProgressEvents\" -> events|>,\n            \"ExampleFailure\"],\n        Quiet[DeleteDirectory[directory, DeleteContents -> True]]\n    ]\n];"], "Input", InitializationCell -> True],

Cell["Run the small CPU example", "Section"],

Cell[BoxData["result = RunSL2CfoamXXExample[\"CPU\"];\nIf[FailureQ[result], result, KeyDrop[result, {\"Tensor\", \"Array\", \"Coefficients\", \"ProgressEvents\"}]]"], "Input"],

Cell["Inspect arrays and progress", "Section"],

Cell["Normal[tensor] creates an independent packed Mathematica array. Tensor positions start at 1. The first slice and the tensor/tensor contraction below are ordinary Mathematica arrays; array operations run on the CPU.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["If[!FailureQ[result], result[\"CoherentAmplitude\"]]"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["If[!FailureQ[result], result[\"Array\"][[1]]]"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["If[!FailureQ[result], result[\"Contraction\"]]"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["If[!FailureQ[result], result[\"ProgressEvents\"]]"], "Input"],

Cell["Optional GPU calculation", "Section"],

Cell["The following cell runs the same small example only when the loaded library has a CUDA backend and a compatible NVIDIA device. Fixed-intertwiner amplitudes and Mathematica array operations remain on the CPU; full-tensor and coherent native computations use the GPU.", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["If[TrueQ[BackendAvailableQ[\"GPU\"]],\n    gpuResult = RunSL2CfoamXXExample[\"GPU\"];\n    If[FailureQ[gpuResult], gpuResult, gpuResult[\"CoherentAmplitude\"]],\n    \"GPU backend unavailable in this kernel; the CPU example remains usable.\"\n]"], "Input"],

Cell["Larger calculations", "Section"],

Cell["The optional call RunSL2CfoamXXExample[\"GPU\", 12, 6] uses physical spin j = 6 and cutoff 6. It can require substantially more time and memory. Change the backend to \"CPU\" to use the CPU implementation; larger calls retain the closure, tensor, persistence and contraction checks, while the fixed numerical reference applies only to the default small example.", "Text"],

Cell["SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Jeremy Martinon\nSPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later", "Text"]
},
WindowSize -> {1000, 800},
WindowTitle -> "sl2cfoam++ Mathematica example",
StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"
]
